## Phase 2: Historical minecart correction (superseded)

This section records the passing custom-screen implementation that preceded
`ds.mountNativeScreen()`. Its user-visible assertions remain requirements, but
their active migration is tracked in `native-dwarfspec-command-migration.todo`.

- [x] Open the native Hauling Routes menu through native screen input.
- [x] Obtain the active `MinecartRouteMarkersOverlay` instance from the DFHack overlay registry.
- [x] Remove the separately constructed overlay instance from the native component test.
- [x] Remove native-test stubs for focus detection and overlay disablement.
- [x] Confirm the registry-created overlay becomes active only while its real focus conditions are satisfied.
- [x] Move the pointer onto route rows and stop rows with DwarfSpec's pointer API.
- [x] Allow the normal render loop to update hover state.
- [x] Remove empty `overlay:onInput({})` calls used to force hover refreshes.
- [x] Click route and stop rows through the mounted screen input path.
- [x] Assert that clicking either row selects the appropriate route in the native menu.
- [x] Assert that the selected-row indicator is rendered at the correct menu-relative position.
- [x] Assert that route-stop world markers and labels are rendered for the selected route.
- [x] Assert that marker position follows viewport movement using the production world-to-UI transform.
- [x] Hover a stop row and assert that its action rail appears at the configured row-relative position.
- [x] Move the pointer from the row onto the rail and assert that the rail remains open.
- [x] Click the zoom action through the rendered button hit target.
- [x] Assert that the viewport centers on the stop and the corresponding route remains selected.
- [x] Scroll while the pointer is over the action rail and assert that the rail consumes the wheel input.
- [x] Scroll while the pointer is over the native route list and assert that the native list scrolls.
- [x] Assert that the rail rebinds to the correct visible row after native list scrolling.
- [x] Assert that stale action callbacks cannot act on a formerly bound stop.

### Completion gate

- [x] The minecart component test uses the registry-created production overlay.
- [x] All pointer movement, clicking, and wheel input use public DwarfSpec APIs.
- [x] Selection indicators, route markers, labels, zoom behavior, rail retention, and scrolling are verified from rendered or native state.
- [x] No direct overlay `onInput()`, forced refresh, or lifecycle stub is required.

